---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Handshake | Claim">
  <section class="py-20 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-8 capitalize">Claim</h1>
      
      <div class="bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-500 p-6 mb-8 rounded-r-lg">
        <div class="flex">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0">
            <svg class="h-6 w-6 text-amber-500" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="ml-3">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-amber-800">Claim Period Ended</h3>
            <div class="mt-2 text-amber-700">
              <p>
                The FOSS developer claim period has officially ended following the recent soft fork. It is no longer possible to claim HNS from the initial airdrop.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-2">
                For more information regarding the network upgrades and the soft fork, please refer to the official <a href="https://github.com/handshake-org/hsd" class="underline font-medium hover:text-amber-900">hsd repository</a> or community channels.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="prose prose-slate prose-lg opacity-50">
        <h2>Legacy Claim Information</h2>
        <p>This page previously contained instructions for FOSS developers to claim their airdrop allocation. As the claim period is now over, these instructions are preserved for historical reference only.</p>
        <p>Original content from legacy/claim/index.html is being preserved and adapted.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
